# LifeQuesT Global

## TypeScript
- Strict mode always. No `any`, no `@ts-ignore` without comment.
- Extend types in `src/types/index.ts` — do not duplicate interfaces.

## Layer boundaries (enforce strictly)
| Layer | May import | Must NOT import |
|-------|-----------|-----------------|
| `engine/` | `types/`, `data/` | `store/`, `services/`, `screens/`, `components/` |
| `store/` | `engine/`, `services/`, `types/`, `data/`, `utils/` | `screens/`, `components/` |
| `services/` | `types/`, `config/`, Firebase SDK | `store/`, `engine/` |
| `screens/` | `store/`, `components/`, `types/`, `navigation/` | `engine/` directly |
| `components/` | `types/`, `theme/`, `constants/` | `store/` (use props) |

## Imports
- Use path aliases (`@store/*`, `@components/*`, etc.) when touching a file.
- Migrate relative `../` imports to aliases in the same edit.
- **Alias parity:** new alias → update `tsconfig.json`, `babel.config.js`, and `jest.config.js` together.

## Expo
- SDK **56** only. Read https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v56.0.0/ before writing Expo/RN code.

## Token efficiency
- Do NOT load `docs/workflows/*` unless the task requires that department.
- Use `.claude/SKILLS_INDEX.md` or `.cursor/skills/` to find playbooks.
- Scope features against `docs/workflows/PROJECT_VISION.md` phases when planning.

## AI config maintenance
When conventions, stacks, or recurring patterns change → follow `meta/maintain-ai-config` skill.
Edit `docs/ai-bootstrap/` only; run `setup.sh` + `validate-ai-config.sh`.
Read `meta-ai-config.mdc` when editing bootstrap, workflows, or AI templates.

## Department routing (read only when needed)
| Task | Rule file |
|------|-----------|
| Screens, components, navigation | `frontend.mdc` |
| Engine, gameData, store | `game-engine.mdc` |
| Services, functions, config | `backend.mdc` |
| Tests, lint, jest | `qa.mdc` |
| Ads, IAP, shop | `monetization.mdc` |
| Types, nav params | `types.mdc` |
| Theme, tailwind | `theme.mdc` |
| App entry, boot order | `app-boot.mdc` |
| Rules, skills, hooks, AI templates | `meta-ai-config.mdc` |
